+    /* WS -- the board's own coarse visibility test, and the ONE place in
+     * the board that hardcodes the 4:3 aspect as a literal instead of
+     * reading a camera field. Its callers SKIP DRAWING entirely on a FALSE:
+     * board/object.c's ObjManOMExec (every board object with a
+     * cullRadius >= 0), and board/masu.c's two space-marker draw loops
+     * (the coloured space tiles and the capsule-space overlay). With the
+     * projection now widened to 1.2f*scale_factor(), a literal 1.2f here
+     * declares "not visible" for everything in the band between the native
+     * and the widened frustum -- i.e. board spaces and props would blink
+     * out along the left/right edges at exactly the aspects this lane
+     * unlocks. Widened by the SAME factor the projection is, so the test
+     * matches the frustum it is meant to approximate. Byte-identical (a
+     * literal 1.2f) when widescreen is disabled. */
+    boundX = (1.2f*mp6_widescreen_scale_factor())*(tanHalfFov*-viewPos.z);
